+# 0.9.6_Hardened_4 Static Hasher Boundary Completion Record
+
+**Version treatment:** owner-approved hardening of the public hashing protocol completed in H3.
+**Amendment class:** OWNER-APPROVED SEMANTIC COMPLETION. H3 remains the immutable predecessor. This
+cut changes only the previously unresolved callable/interface representation of `Hash.hash`; it does
+not change the remaining hashing, equality, collection, ownership, borrowing, ABI, effect, reload,
+or determinism contracts.
+
+**Resolved contract.** `Hash.hash` is generic over `H: Hasher`. The concrete argument type is
+inferred and normally monomorphized through the existing generic/interface machinery. Bare `Hasher`
+is not treated as a concrete parameter type, and no implicit `dyn` conversion is introduced.
+`DefaultHasher` implements `Hasher`. Runtime-polymorphic hashing remains available only to a future
+API that explicitly specifies a legal `dyn Hasher` representation.
+
+**Evidence boundary.** This specification completion does not claim compiler or conformance support
+for the public hashing surface. Executable status remains external repository evidence.
 
